				<property name='Compressor' folder='property_1' hidden='0' >
					<property name='Processing' target='Processing' typeid='10' hidden='0' locked='1' info='Set automatically from the buffer type.
8 and 16-bit integer buffers use fixed point maths with no floating point library, ideal for 8-bit devices.
32-bit integer and float buffers use floating point maths.' />
					<property name='Signal Centre' target='SignalCentre' typeid='15' hidden='1' locked='0' info='Value representing a zero signal. Levels are measured as the distance from this value.
Use 0 for signed or float buffers, or the mid point for unsigned data.' />
					<property name='Threshold' target='InitThreshold' typeid='15' hidden='1' locked='0' info='Level, measured from the signal centre, above which compression starts.
Uses the same units as the buffer data.' />
					<property name='Ratio' target='InitRatio' typeid='15' hidden='1' locked='0' info='Amount of compression applied above the threshold, e.g. 4 = 4:1.
A level 4dB above the threshold comes out 1dB above it.
1 = no compression, large values (20+) act as a limiter.' />
					<property name='Attack Time (ms)' target='InitAttack' typeid='15' hidden='1' locked='0' info='Time constant for the compressor to react to a signal rising above the threshold. 0 = instant.' />
					<property name='Release Time (ms)' target='InitRelease' typeid='15' hidden='1' locked='0' info='Time constant for the compressor to recover once the signal level falls. 0 = instant.' />
					<property name='Signal Centre' target='IntCentre' typeid='14' hidden='0' locked='0' info='Value representing a zero signal. Levels are measured as the distance from this value.
Use 0 for signed buffers, or the mid point for unsigned data, e.g. 512 for a 10-bit ADC or 128 for 8-bit data.' />
					<property name='Threshold' target='IntThreshold' typeid='14' hidden='0' locked='0' info='Level, measured from the signal centre, above which compression starts. 1 to 65535.
Uses the same units as the buffer data.' />
					<property name='Ratio' target='IntRatio' typeid='16' hidden='0' locked='0' info='Amount of compression applied above the threshold.
Fixed point mode works on the linear signal level: the part of the level above the threshold is divided by the ratio.
Limiter holds the level at the threshold.' filter='0002:1
0014:1
0028:1
00316:1
00432:1
005Limiter' />
					<property name='Attack Shift' target='IntAttackShift' typeid='14' hidden='0' locked='0' info='Attack time constant as a power of two number of samples, 0 to 15.
0 = instant, 1 = 2 samples, 2 = 4 samples, 3 = 8 samples ...
Shifts are used in place of multiplies to keep the maths fast on 8-bit devices.' />
					<property name='Attack Time (ms)' target='IntAttackTime' typeid='15' hidden='0' locked='1' info='Attack time constant resulting from the attack shift at the specified sample rate.' />
					<property name='Release Shift' target='IntReleaseShift' typeid='14' hidden='0' locked='0' info='Release time constant as a power of two number of samples, 0 to 15.
0 = instant, 1 = 2 samples, 2 = 4 samples, 3 = 8 samples ...' />
					<property name='Release Time (ms)' target='IntReleaseTime' typeid='15' hidden='0' locked='1' info='Release time constant resulting from the release shift at the specified sample rate.' />
					<property name='Makeup Gain' target='InitMakeup' typeid='15' hidden='0' locked='0' info='Linear gain multiplier applied after compression to restore the overall level. 1 = no change.
In fixed point mode this is converted to a 1/256 step value when compiled, maximum 32.' />
					<property name='Sample Rate (Hz)' target='SampleRate' typeid='15' hidden='0' locked='0' info='Rate at which samples are passed through the compressor.
Used to convert between attack and release times and samples.' />
					<property name='Ratio Shift' target='IntRatioShift' typeid='14' hidden='1' locked='0' info='' />
